    "https://employment.potsdam.edu/postings/5518": {
      "title": "SUNY Potsdam Employment Site",
      "description": "SUNY Potsdam Employment Site | Counselor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Counselor Bookmark this Recruitment Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For other document 1, please upload a document with contact information for three professional references. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number: U - 00662 Position Title: Counselor Local Title: Counselor Job Category Professional/Management FLSA Classification: Exempt Obligation: College Year If College Year, Please fill in period of no obligation: 1 month as approved by supervisor. Position Type Term Appointment Start date: Appointment End date : Salary: $67,500 Salary Grade: SL3 Full Time or Part Time: Full Time If Part-Time, fill in %: Benefits Summary UUP Full-time Benefits Summary Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program ( PSLF ) Department Information Department: COUNSELING CENTER Division Student Affairs Search Contact Information Search Contact(s): Amy Richardson Search Contact Phone/Extension: 315-267-2257 Search Contact Email: richaral@potsdam.edu Search Contact Fax: Posting Text Job Summary/Basic Function: SUNY Potsdam’s College Counseling Center is committed to providing high-quality, confidential, ethical, and culturally affirming mental health services to SUNY Potsdam students. Staff members work as a collaborative team to offer services from an integrated clinical/developmental model to assist students as they pursue their education while in attendance during the semester. The Counseling Center at SUNY Potsdam invites applications for a 11-month, full-time, Staff Counselor position. The counselor will provide a wide range of clinical services at this comprehensive counseling center, including triage, individual and group psychotherapy, consultation, and crisis assessment/response. The position includes weekend and weekday after-hours responsibilities on a rotating basis. In addition, case management responsibilities for all students using the services will include coordination and communication with off-campus mental health providers and on-campus resources. Job Requirements & Essential Functions of the Job: Make referrals to off-campus providers and facilities, when needed, and coordinate the readmission process for students away from campus for psychological reasons. Participate in outreach programming, training with student groups, and occasional campus committee participation. Respond to inquiries from parents, staff, and faculty regarding Counseling Center services. Maintain scheduling and clinical documentation on Counseling Center database. Teach the Peer Counseling course and provide ongoing supervision and mentorship to peer counselors completing their internship, including training, case consultation, skill development, and evaluation of counseling competencies. Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in Mental Health Counseling or Social Work License eligible in New York State ( LMHC , LMSW , L- CSW , MHC -LP, MSW ) Experience providing services to diverse and inclusive populations. Prior counseling and psychotherapy experience with college-aged students. Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills, including writing skills, with an emphasis on timely and thorough documentation. Prior experience in dealing with crisis situations. Ability to follow through and work both independently as well as part of a team with a positive attitude. Previous experience in providing case management services. Effective use and management of multiple technological tools (e.g., Electronic Health Records, PowerPoint, social media applications, tele-counseling software). We are seeking candidates who possess communication and interpersonal skills sufficient to work effectively with an increasingly diverse array of students and colleagues and who have demonstrated a commitment to creating, fostering and sustaining an inclusive environment in and out of the classroom. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience at a college/university counseling center with short term therapy models. LMHC , LMSW , LCSW or LCSW -R We are, especially, seeking candidates who have engaged in professional development activities to enhance knowledge of diversity, equity and inclusion and have worked collaboratively across various departments in fostering success of underrepresented groups and a supportive and inclusive environment for all. Supervisor: David Nelson, LCSW-R Location: Van Housen Hall Posting Detail Information Close Date: Open Until Filled Yes EEO Information All people with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Special Instructions to Applicants: For other document 1, please upload a document with contact information for three professional references. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this opening? Please be specific. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a NYS Mental Health Counselor/Clinical Social Worker license? Yes No * If you heard about this job posting on social media, please indicate what platform: Facebook LinkedIn Instagram Other Not Applicable Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Other Document 1 (Refer to job posting detail information for special instructions.) Optional Documents © 2020 SUNY Potsdam The State University of New York at Potsdam, all rights reserved. 44 Pierrepont Avenue | Potsdam, NY 13676 | 315-267-2000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
