    "https://employment.potsdam.edu/postings/5516": {
      "title": "SUNY Potsdam Employment Site | College Physician&#39;s Assistant",
      "description": "SUNY Potsdam Employment Site | College Physician&#39;s Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources College Physician's Assistant Bookmark this Recruitment Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please upload a document with the names and contact information for 3 professional references as Other Document 1. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number: U - 00660 Position Title: College Physician's Assistant Local Title: Psychiatric Nurse Practitioner Job Category Professional/Management FLSA Classification: Exempt Obligation: College Year If College Year, Please fill in period of no obligation: 11-month obligation with no obligation from 12/21/2026 through 1/17/2027 Position Type Term Appointment Start date: 08/24/2026 Appointment End date : Salary: $110,000 Salary Grade: SL3 Full Time or Part Time: Full Time If Part-Time, fill in %: Benefits Summary Department Information Department: STUDENT HEALTH Division Student Affairs Search Contact Information Search Contact(s): Amy L. Richardson Director of Student Health and Counseling Services Search Contact Phone/Extension: 315-267-2330 Search Contact Email: richaral@potsdam.edu Search Contact Fax: 315-267-3260 Posting Text Job Summary/Basic Function: Provision of primary care medicine to students, including assessment, diagnosis, and the implementation of a treatment plan in accordance with a collaborative relationship with the Director of Student Health Services. Emphasis is placed on primary prevention and health/wellness education. Reports to the Director of Student Health Services. Job Requirements & Essential Functions of the Job: Psychiatric Nurse Practitioner (Full-Time) SUNY Potsdam is seeking a full-time Psychiatric Nurse Practitioner ( PMHNP ) to provide high-quality, student-centered psychiatric care within the College Counseling Center. The Psychiatric Nurse Practitioner will serve as an integral member of a multidisciplinary behavioral health team, providing comprehensive psychiatric assessment, diagnosis, psychotherapy, medication management, consultation, and education to support the mental health and well-being of SUNY Potsdam students. The successful candidate will demonstrate professionalism, clinical excellence, sound judgment, and a commitment to SUNY Potsdam’s mission, vision, and values while adhering to all institutional policies, ethical standards, and applicable federal and New York State regulations. The Psychiatric Nurse Practitioner will protect students’ autonomy, dignity, rights, values, and beliefs while providing compassionate, culturally responsive, trauma-informed care. Key Responsibilities Conduct comprehensive psychiatric evaluations, including assessment of mental health conditions, psychosocial functioning, trauma history, and risk factors. Assess, diagnose, and treat mental health disorders in individuals using evidence-based psychiatric practices. Develop, implement, monitor, and revise individualized treatment plans. Prescribe, adjust, and monitor psychotropic medications while evaluating therapeutic effectiveness and potential side effects. Provide psychotherapy, supportive counseling, psychoeducation, and brief therapeutic interventions appropriate to the college population. Educate students and, when appropriate, their families about mental health conditions, treatment options, medications, and strategies that promote recovery and wellness. Counsel students regarding healthy lifestyle practices and behaviors that support emotional well-being and treatment outcomes. Consult and collaborate with counseling center clinicians, primary care providers, Student Health Services staff, and other campus and community partners to coordinate comprehensive care. Participate in case consultations and interdisciplinary treatment planning. Evaluate students’ functional status and provide recommendations regarding medical leaves of absence, return-to-campus planning, academic accommodations, and other clinically indicated interventions. Maintain timely, accurate, and complete clinical documentation in the electronic health record in accordance with professional standards, legal requirements, and institutional policies. Contribute to program development, quality improvement initiatives, clinical policy development, and other program management activities. Communicate effectively with members of the multidisciplinary healthcare team while maintaining appropriate confidentiality. Apply ethical principles and professional standards in all aspects of clinical decision-making. Treat students, families, colleagues, and campus partners with respect, dignity, compassion, and cultural sensitivity. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrated expertise in psychiatric assessment, diagnosis, and treatment of mental health disorders. Strong knowledge of psychopharmacology and evidence-based psychiatric interventions. Ability to provide both psychotherapy and medication management. Knowledge of clinical interviewing, mental status examinations, and behavioral health assessment techniques. Excellent clinical judgment, critical thinking, and problem-solving skills. Strong communication, interpersonal, and active listening skills. Ability to collaborate effectively within a multidisciplinary healthcare team. Ability to establish therapeutic relationships with a diverse college student population. Commitment to ethical practice, cultural humility, trauma-informed care, and student-centered treatment. Preferred Personal Characteristics Compassionate and empathetic approach to patient care. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Patience, professionalism, and sound clinical judgment. Dedication to student well-being and high-quality patient care. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively as a collaborative member of an interdisciplinary team. Commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and serving the unique mental health needs of college students. Required Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Current New York State licensure (or eligibility for licensure) as a Registered Professional Nurse and certification as a Nurse Practitioner in Psychiatry (Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner) by the New York State Education Department. Current DEA registration and New York State authority to prescribe controlled substances (or eligibility to obtain). National certification as a Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner ( PMHNP -BC) from the ANCC . Experience providing psychiatric assessment, psychotherapy, and medication management. We are seeking candidates who possess communication and interpersonal skills sufficient to work effectively with an increasingly diverse array of students and colleagues and who have demonstrated a commitment to creating, fostering and sustaining an inclusive environment in and out of the classroom. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with diverse population. Experience with college population. We are, especially, seeking candidates who have engaged in professional development activities to enhance knowledge of diversity, equity and inclusion and have worked collaboratively across various departments in fostering success of underrepresented groups and a supportive and inclusive environment for all. Supervisor: Alicia Sienkiewycz, FNP-C, PMHNP-BC Location: SUNY Potsdam Student Health Services Posting Detail Information Close Date: Open Until Filled Yes EEO Information SUNY Potsdam is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race including traits historically associated with race, color, national origin including ancestry, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity or expression, actual or perceived sexual orientation, citizenship or immigration status, familial status, marital status, pregnancy, genetic information, predisposing genetic characteristics, military status, domestic violence victim status, criminal conviction, or any other characteristic protected under applicable state or federal law. All qualified applicants with disabilities may be entitled to reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York State Human Rights Law, or other applicable state and federal laws. We will consider requests for reasonable accommodation from qualified applicants with disabilities in completing this application or to otherwise participate in the application process, or, should they be selected to be interviewed, to facilitate their interview. Applicants with disabilities may contact Human Resources to discuss, in confidence, any request for reasonable accommodations. Executive Order 161: Pursuant to Executive Order 161, no State entity, as defined by the Executive Order, is permitted to ask, or mandate, in any form, that an applicant for employment provide his or her current compensation, or any prior compensation history, until such time as the applicant is extended a conditional offer of employment with compensation. If such information has been requested from you before such time, please contact the Governor’s Office of Employee Relations at (518) 474-6988 or via email at info@goer.ny.gov<mailto:info@goer.ny.gov>. All people with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Special Instructions to Applicants: Please upload a document with the names and contact information for 3 professional references as Other Document 1. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this opening? Please be specific. (Open Ended Question) * If you heard about this job posting on social media, please indicate what platform: Facebook LinkedIn Instagram Other Not Applicable Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Other Document 1 (Refer to job posting detail information for special instructions.) Optional Documents © 2020 SUNY Potsdam The State University of New York at Potsdam, all rights reserved. 44 Pierrepont Avenue | Potsdam, NY 13676 | 315-267-2000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
