    "https://employment.potsdam.edu/postings/5507": {
      "title": "SUNY Potsdam Employment Site | Visiting Assistant Professor",
      "description": "SUNY Potsdam Employment Site | Visiting Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Visiting Assistant Professor Bookmark this Recruitment Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For other document 1, please upload a document with the name and contact information for three professional references. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number: U - 00647 Position Title: Visiting Assistant Professor Local Title: Visiting Assistant Professor - Computer Science Job Category Faculty FLSA Classification: Obligation: Academic Year If College Year, Please fill in period of no obligation: Position Type Temporary Appointment Start date: Appointment End date : Salary: $28,000 Salary Grade: Full Time or Part Time: Part Time If Part-Time, fill in %: 50% Benefits Summary UUP Part-time Benefits Summary Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) Department Information Department: COMPUTER SCIENCE Division Academic Affairs Search Contact Information Search Contact(s): Dr. Supraja Gurajala, Associate Professor, Computer Science Search Contact Phone/Extension: 315-267-2091 Search Contact Email: gurajas@potsdam.edu Search Contact Fax: Posting Text Job Summary/Basic Function: The State University of New York, Potsdam ( SUNY Potsdam), seeks applicants for a half-time Visiting Assistant Professor position in Computer Science beginning in Fall 2026. The successful candidate will join a small, engaged department and contribute to Bachelor of Science tracks in cybersecurity and machine learning, teaching across the computer science curriculum. The specific area of specialization is open. The position is open until filled. Job Requirements & Essential Functions of the Job: The successful candidate must be able and willing to teach introductory and core computer science courses at all levels. Responsibilities include teaching 2 courses and 3 lab sections or similar load per academic year. Responsibilities may also include teaching courses online, at our extension sites, or in the general education program. Required Qualifications: An earned PhD in Computer Science from an accredited institution. ABD candidates will be seriously considered. We are seeking candidates who possess communication and interpersonal skills sufficient to work effectively with an increasingly diverse array of students and colleagues and who have demonstrated a commitment to creating, fostering and sustaining an inclusive environment in and out of the classroom. Preferred Qualifications: Preference will be given to candidates with experience teaching computer science courses at the college level. The ability to teach introductory computer science, cybersecurity, machine learning, artificial intelligence, or software engineering is desirable. We are, especially, seeking candidates who have worked with, done research with, or taught under-represented groups and have worked collaboratively across various departments in fostering success of underrepresented groups. Supervisor: Dr. Laura Grabowski Location: Posting Detail Information Close Date: Open Until Filled Yes EEO Information All people with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Special Instructions to Applicants: For other document 1, please upload a document with the name and contact information for three professional references. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this opening? Please be specific. (Open Ended Question) * If you heard about this job posting on social media, please indicate what platform: Facebook LinkedIn Instagram Other Not Applicable Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Other Document 1 (Refer to job posting detail information for special instructions.) Optional Documents Unofficial Transcript 1 © 2020 SUNY Potsdam The State University of New 